Z||000005||Uaana||10-18-2001||04:36 PM||||The only thing I looked into was the seats from a 1st Gen MR2. (leather, side and lower lumbar adjustments ect ect all the nice things GM is to cheap to put in a seat)<BR>problem was the rails <BR>Fiero rails are 13.5in apart and the MR2's were about 17.25 in apart. It's probably very doable if you have some welding skills.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||10-18-2001||05:43 PM||||I really like the Del Sol; if they came with a larger engine from the factory or were more affordable with a more powerful motor, I would already have one.  I can't believe how people hear Honda and automatically think "ricer"....I guess I thought that ricer didn't mean "well engineered"...<P>I know I'm going to hear back about this, but I think a fully modded del sol looks just as good as a fully modded fiero.  It's a bonus that there is a strong aftermarket following for those....especially for the "latest" parts.  Given, there are more wanna-be del sols than should be acceptable, but there are also some very nice ones.  A huge plus, in my mind, is the factory targa option and the roll-down back window.  This basically forms a convertible, without many of the drawbacks.<P>Just my two cents as well.  I don't think many honda dashes have too much style, but they are almost always much much better quality than american.  If I was going to work on a custom interior, I'd use a factory dash and just start hacking, bondoing, fiberglass, and finessing it to how I wanted it.<P>Good luck.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||10-18-2001||05:47 PM||||I'll definitely agree with you on the well-engineered comment.  Especially on the Targa top & back window- that's really quite cool, and I'd say better overall than most convertibles. I'm not a huge fan of the rest of the styling... not quite exotic enough- but still pretty cool.  I'm not real familiar with whether or not you can get much power from them without replacing the motor (I know in GranToursimo 2 you can get a DelSol with 650hp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).||||reg||1
Z||000008||FLASHY||10-18-2001||06:17 PM||||I've seen some pretty cool modified ones. I totally agree with Nashco.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||gangrenefiero||10-18-2001||06:38 PM||||The del sols did come with a big engine too. The DOHC Vtec goes 0-60 in 6.9, my roommate has one and we race but he wins. But im working on it. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||rmorgandotcom||10-18-2001||11:09 PM||||I think it be cool if they had made the Del Sol mid-engined (I look at my uncles and I think that it has a huge trunk!).  For the interior, me and my dad are going with a mostly hand-built custom dash.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rmorgansig.jpg">   <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI><I><FONT COLOR="blue">project - finale body on a 86 4 cylinder 5 speed</FONT></I><BR><LI><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/</A><BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000011||yo_sweet||10-19-2001||12:32 AM||||itz still a butt ugly car even when all done up with fart can exausht and what not the Fiero GTs are much nicer<P>ps this jaei sun guy is into rice a little to much for comfort<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE<BR>customized tail light's,american raceing rim's,k&n air filter,pioneer cd player.. more to come<P>kill's: 1990 Honda CRX,93 ACURA integra, 85 mr2,94 pontiac grand am,94 mustang, suzuki swift 5 car lengths!,86 laser 4cyl.<P>loses: 1996 camero Z28,2000 grand prix 3.8L, 1986 monty carlo SS||||reg||1
Z||000012||FLASHY||10-19-2001||10:35 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||10-19-2001||11:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>...this jaei sun guy is into rice a little to much for comfort<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've met jaei sun- and he's a cool guy. Definitely not at all your "typical" ricer type (no stickers on his car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).<P>You've got to give credit where credit is due. It's really quite impressive to be able to make an import 4-banger put out 400+hp without swapping the motor (when was the last time you saw a duke dyno out at 400hp?).  And if you don't mod it, it'll easily outlast most American engines (My 2.8 only lasted 98k miles and died a slow death with lots of black smoke and oil).  Now I'm not defending the "ricer" concept- stickers are not cool, 4-door sedans are not (usually) cool, but a 2-door (eclipse, supra, etc...) that can run 10's at the track, then drive home is pretty impressive.<P>And what's wrong with a little "rice" style anyway? I'm making clear taillights & indiglo gauges for my GT... and I even like some of the big "ricer" wings.<P>Now I'm not flaming here, just spewing my opinion to all who will listen (hello?  is anyone still reading this?  darn...).<P>If you really want to see what not to do with your cars... and the cars that I truly laugh at- check out <A HREF="http://www.beaterz.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.beaterz.com</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  that's all.||||reg||1
Z||000014||DXR_DAD||10-19-2001||12:09 PM||||MinnGreen, THANK YOU. I own a Del Sol. And if you ask anyone here that knows me they will tell you I'm no were near a "ricer"!!!! I'm just a guy that lover CARS!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=53093152&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723600&p=53090206&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P>DXR_DAD<P><BR>||||reg||14
