Z||000016||ChopTop||10-19-2001||12:54 PM||||Add my name to the Del Sol like list.  Only thing I don't care for is the thick rear pillar.  Which is what our coupes would look like if there wasn't a simulated window there.  I'm quite surprised Honda overlooked that detail.  I remember reading Pontiac designers weren't real happy with having to put a fake window on, but felt it would look better to have a fake window than no window.  Seems I also read the Asian version had a power top.  The rear trunk lid raises straight up, the targa section slides into it like a drawer, and the trunk then lowers back down, pretty neat.  I think a dropped and chopped one would look great.||||reg||1
